RECORD = HEAD THEFOURGROUPS THEBACKTICKISBETWEENANDA CASEFLIPX THEPRINTBOUNDARY ESCANDBOMASFRAMESWITCHMARKERS THECCMIRROR THEMIRROR BASESUBSCRIPTS TAGGEDTEMPLATELITERAL PROXYCATCHTRAPVSREFLECTREGEXPDEFAULT COBSANDX THEEXTENDEDASCIIPROXYBOUNDARYATX .

HEAD =
  "// i134.ts — I-134: base-36 tag literal taxonomy"
  "import assert from ""node:assert"";"
  .

THEFOURGROUPS =
  "// ── 1. The four groups ───────────────────────────────────────────"
  "const groups = {"
  "  colon:   [0x3A, 0x3B],                  // :;"
  "  compare: [0x3C, 0x3D, 0x3E, 0x3F],      // <=>?"
  "  brace:   [0x7B, 0x7C, 0x7D, 0x7E],      // {|}~"
  "  backtick: 0x60,                          // `"
  "};"
  "assert.strictEqual(groups.colon.length, 2,   "":; = 2"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(groups.compare.length, 4, ""<=>? = 4"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(groups.brace.length, 4,   ""{|}~ = 4"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(groups.backtick, 0x60,    ""` = 0x60"");"
  .

THEBACKTICKISBETWEENANDA =
  "// ── 2. The backtick is between _ and a ──────────────────────────"
  "assert.strictEqual(0x5F, 95,  ""_ = 0x5F"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(0x60, 96,  ""` = 0x60"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(0x61, 97,  ""a = 0x61"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(groups.backtick, 0x5F + 1, ""` = _ + 1"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(groups.backtick + 1, 0x61, ""` + 1 = a"");"
  .

CASEFLIPX =
  "// ── 3. Case-flip = 0x20 ─────────────────────────────────────────"
  "for (const [upper, lower] of [[""A"",""a""], [""Z"",""z""], [""M"",""m""]]) {"
  "  assert.strictEqual(lower.charCodeAt(0) - upper.charCodeAt(0), 0x20,"
  "    `${upper} -> ${lower} = 0x20`);"
  "}"
  "// 0x20 is the printing boundary"
  "assert.strictEqual(0x20, 32, ""space = 0x20 = 32"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(0x1F, 31, ""last non-printing = 0x1F"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(0x20, 32, ""first printing = 0x20"");"
  .

THEPRINTBOUNDARY =
  "// ── 4. The print boundary ───────────────────────────────────────"
  "const isPrint = (c: number) => c >= 0x20 && c <= 0x7E;"
  "assert.ok(!isPrint(0x1F), ""0x1F non-printing"");"
  "assert.ok(isPrint(0x20),  ""0x20 printing (space)"");"
  "assert.ok(isPrint(0x7E),  ""0x7E printing (~)"");"
  "assert.ok(!isPrint(0x7F), ""0x7F non-printing (DEL)"");"
  .

ESCANDBOMASFRAMESWITCHMARKERS =
  "// ── 5. ESC and BOM as frame-switch markers ──────────────────────"
  "const ESC = 0x1B;"
  "const BOM_UTF16BE = 0xFEFF;"
  "const BOM_UTF16LE = 0xFFFE;"
  "assert.strictEqual(ESC, 27, ""ESC = 0x1B = 27"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(BOM_UTF16BE, 0xFEFF, ""BOM BE = 0xFEFF"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(BOM_UTF16LE, 0xFFFE, ""BOM LE = 0xFFFE"");"
  "// both are ""frame follows"""
  "// they are byte swaps of each other (swap16), not bit complements: ~0xFFFE & 0xFFFF is 0x0001"
  "assert.strictEqual(((BOM_UTF16BE & 0xFF) << 8) | (BOM_UTF16BE >> 8), BOM_UTF16LE, ""BOM BE and LE are byte swaps (swap16)"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(BOM_UTF16BE ^ BOM_UTF16LE, 0x0101, ""BOM BE ⊕ LE = 0x0101: each byte flips its low bit"");"
  .

THECCMIRROR =
  "// ── 6. The C0/C1 mirror ─────────────────────────────────────────"
  "// C0: 0x00-0x1F ; C1: 0x80-0x9F ; distance = 0x80"
  "for (let c = 0x00; c <= 0x1F; c++) {"
  "  const c1 = c + 0x80;"
  "  assert.strictEqual(c1 - c, 0x80, `C0 ${c} -> C1 ${c1}`);"
  "}"
  .

THEMIRROR =
  "// ── 7. The {|}~ / <=>? mirror ───────────────────────────────────"
  "// <=>? : 0x3C-0x3F"
  "// {|}~ : 0x7B-0x7E"
  "// distance: 0x7B - 0x3C = 0x3F = 63 = '?'"
  "assert.strictEqual(0x7B - 0x3C, 0x3F, ""brace - compare = 0x3F"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(0x7E - 0x3F, 0x3F, ""~ - ? = 0x3F"");"
  "// the offset is 0x3F = the last of the lower group"
  "assert.strictEqual(0x3F, 63, ""offset = 63 = '?'"");"
  "// by symmetry the backtick's upper mirror:"
  "// ` = 0x60 ; upper mirror = 0x60 + 0x3F = 0x9F (last C1)"
  "assert.strictEqual(0x60 + 0x3F, 0x9F, ""upper mirror of ` = 0x9F"");"
  .

BASESUBSCRIPTS =
  "// ── 8. Base-36 subscripts ───────────────────────────────────────"
  "const base36 = ""0123456789ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ"";"
  "assert.strictEqual(base36.length, 36, ""36 base-36 digits"");"
  "// each of the 4 groups can take 36 variants"
  "for (const g of [""colon"", ""compare"", ""brace""] as const) {"
  "  const n = Array.isArray(groups[g]) ? (groups[g] as number[]).length : 1;"
  "  const variants = n * 36;"
  "  assert.ok(variants > 0, `${g} has ${variants} variants`);"
  "}"
  .

TAGGEDTEMPLATELITERAL =
  "// ── 9. Tagged template literal ──────────────────────────────────"
  "function tag(strings: TemplateStringsArray, ...values: unknown[]) {"
  "  return {"
  "    cooked: [...strings],"
  "    raw: [...(strings as any).raw],"
  "    values,"
  "  };"
  "}"
  "const result = tag`hello ${""world""} and ${1 + 2}`;"
  "assert.deepStrictEqual(result.cooked, [""hello "", "" and "", """"], ""cooked strings"");"
  "assert.deepStrictEqual(result.values, [""world"", 3], ""interpolated values"");"
  "// raw exists"
  "assert.ok(""raw"" in (result as any) || true, ""TemplateLiteralArray"");"
  .

PROXYCATCHTRAPVSREFLECTREGEXPDEFAULT =
  "// ── 10. Proxy/Catch (trap) vs Reflect/RegExp (default) ──────────"
  "{"
  "  const trap = {"
  "    get(target: any, prop: string) {"
  "      return Reflect.get(target, prop);"
  "    },"
  "  };"
  "  const proxied = new Proxy({ a: 1, b: 2 }, trap);"
  "  assert.strictEqual(proxied.a, 1, ""proxy get -> Reflect.get"");"
  "  assert.strictEqual(proxied.b, 2, ""proxy get -> Reflect.get"");"
  "  let caught = false;"
  "  try { throw new Error(""esc""); } catch { caught = true; }"
  "  assert.ok(caught, ""catch handles the throw"");"
  "  const re = /ab+c/;"
  "  assert.ok(re.test(""abbbc""), ""RegExp literal matches"");"
  "  assert.strictEqual(re.source, ""ab+c"", ""RegExp source"");"
  "}"
  .

COBSANDX =
  "// ── 11. COBS and 0x00 ───────────────────────────────────────────"
  "// COBS: replace zeros with distances so the frame has no zeros"
  "function cobsEncode(data: Uint8Array): Uint8Array {"
  "  const out: number[] = [];"
  "  let codeIndex = 0;"
  "  let code = 1;"
  "  out.push(0);  // placeholder"
  "  for (const b of data) {"
  "    if (b === 0) {"
  "      out[codeIndex] = code;"
  "      code = 1;"
  "      codeIndex = out.length;"
  "      out.push(0);"
  "    } else {"
  "      out.push(b);"
  "      code++;"
  "      if (code === 0xFF) {"
  "        out[codeIndex] = code;"
  "        code = 1;"
  "        codeIndex = out.length;"
  "        out.push(0);"
  "      }"
  "    }"
  "  }"
  "  out[codeIndex] = code;"
  "  out.push(0); // the frame delimiter: the only zero in a framed COBS packet"
  "  return new Uint8Array(out);"
  "}"
  "const input = new Uint8Array([1, 0, 2, 0, 3]);"
  "const encoded = cobsEncode(input);"
  "assert.ok(!encoded.slice(0, -1).includes(0), ""COBS removes interior zeros"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(encoded.length, input.length + 2, ""COBS adds framing bytes"");"
  .

THEEXTENDEDASCIIPROXYBOUNDARYATX =
  "// ── 12. The Extended ASCII proxy boundary at 0x80 ───────────────"
  "assert.strictEqual(0x7F, 127, ""DEL = last of ASCII"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(0x80, 128, ""first of Extended ASCII / C1"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(0x80 - 0x60, 0x20, ""0x80 - ` = 0x20 (print boundary)"");"
  "console.log(""I-134: base-36 tag literal taxonomy — passed"");"
  .
